q=v['primary'];lo,hi=q['conservative95IntervalPP'];para('Halftime coaching<br/>Matched-availability workload validation',h);para('<b>18 November 2026 | Completed, audited and independently recomputed</b>')
para('The unchanged boundary-corrected candidate completed <b>576 paired cases / 1,152 full matches</b>. Both teams had the same available-player count and starting tempo, pressure and running workload. Four synthetic roster templates, three small opponent-quality offsets, two availability levels and three workload roots formed 18 contexts. Eight fresh seeds per profile balanced the original simulation side.')
para(f"The focal policy won <b>{q['policyWins']}/576 ({100*q['policyWins']/576:.2f}%)</b>, versus <b>{q['holdWins']}/576 ({100*q['holdWins']/576:.2f}%)</b> for Hold. The pre-match win-rate difference was <b>{q['winChangePP']:+.2f} percentage points</b>, with the prospective conservative 95% interval <b>{lo:+.2f} to {hi:+.2f}</b>. Winners changed toward the focal team in {q['changedToFocal']} cases and against it in {q['changedAgainstFocal']}.")
para(f"The policy changed tactics in <b>{q['changes']}/576 ({100*q['changes']/576:.1f}%)</b>. Its mean final-score-margin difference was {q['meanMarginChange']:+.2f} score points. These are isolated, fixed-matrix estimates; no earlier study or original-policy outcome was pooled. An interval containing zero is not proof of benefit, non-inferiority or safety.")
